**How to implement.** The code seed values go, and with them the stores that seed themselves (001 §B: 'then the Domain seed values are deleted'; 001 §R 'The code seed values and seedAll's Domain source'; .spec-md §3.3). The well-known ids stay: `MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds` and `CatalogueIds`, read by the default-scene prebinds, the colour maps and the tests. Nothing reads a seed any more (steps 46-57). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `standardCategories`, `builtInEntries`, `standard`, the private complexities of the built-ins and every private helper only they use (the `ConstantEpsValue.constantComplexity` extension and any interval or index value left for them) are deleted, and so is the self-seeding `CategoryProxy.createInMemory`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `SeedSamples`, `SeedSources`, `seedEntries`, `sampleLeaf`, `seedTrees` and the self-seeding `createInMemory` are deleted, with the private builders only they use (`filmStructure`, `plateStructure`, `euvLayerThickness`); `qwGlassThickness` and `qwVacuumThickness` stay for `starterMultilayerStructure`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs` and `SampleStore.fs`: the self-seeding `MaterialProxy.createInMemory` and `SampleProxy.createInMemory` are deleted. (4) The plain names are free now, so each empty store takes it (the S1.7 brief; ELEV015 / ELEV019 hold, one member per receiver and one free `createInMemory`): `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty`, `SampleProxy.createInMemoryEmpty`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemoryEmpty` and `Library.createInMemoryEmpty` become `createInMemory` with unchanged signatures and bodies, and every caller follows: `CatalogueImport.fs` (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory`), the fixture `BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 45) and `MainWorkbenchTests` (step 48); a doc naming `createInMemoryEmpty` (the Domain store docs, `CatalogueFiles.fs`' in-memory double) names `createInMemory`. Step 56 left no caller of a self-seeding store, and before the rename `git grep -n -E "(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory " -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor` MUST list only the declarations and docs this step edits (S1.6 steps 42 and 44 and step 49 removed the product's calls), so every renamed call means what it meant; a call anywhere else is a missed re-point and stops the step with its question. (5) Docs and comments say what is true, in no more words: the `MaterialLibrary` and `Library` module docs; `MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `MaterialId`, `CategoryId`, `SampleId`, `SampleIds` and `PresetIds`, which become the identities of the Built-in catalogue's entries (spec 0050 §3.3); the category and store docs that described a seeded catalogue or a self-seeding store; `MaterialVersionId.firstOf` and `SampleVersionId.firstOf`; `LibraryEntryStore`; `liveLibrary`; the `open` comments in `CatalogueImport.fs`; and any `LibraryFacets.fs` doc naming a deleted value. (6) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE' (`AGENTS.md:574-578`): the presets are the preset store that `AppContext.create` fills from the Built-in catalogue (`Catalogue/Builtin/`, `CatalogueImportProxy.importFrom`), and the built-in lasers and UV / EUV lithography sources are protected presets named by `PresetIds`. No seed, no seeding helper and no compatibility alias is kept, and `open`s nothing needs go.

**Acceptance.** After the deletion, `git grep -n -E "SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|allSeedSamples|allSeedSources" -- Berreman/ AGENTS.md` MUST find nothing; `git grep -n -E "let (builtInEntries|seedEntries|standardCategories) " -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` (001 §T 'From section 1') MUST find nothing; `git grep -n -F "createInMemoryEmpty" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; `MaterialLibrary.fs` MUST NOT declare `standard`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
